review_comment:
_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**DRY up identical `transform` pipelines**

`posts`, `changelog`, `careers`, and `policy` all duplicate the same three‑step transform:

1. `compileMDX`
2. return `{ ...document, mdx, slug }` (plus a couple of extras in *posts*)

Maintenance will be easier if these are extracted into a helper, e.g.:

```ts diff
+const makeTransform = (additions: (doc: any) => Record<string, unknown> = () => ({})) =>
+  async (document, context) => {
+    const mdx = await compileMDX(context, document, {
+      remarkPlugins: [remarkGfm, remarkHeading, remarkStructure],
+    });
+    return { ...document, mdx, slug: document._meta.path, ...additions(document) };
+  };

 const posts = defineCollection({
   ...
-  transform: async (document, context) => { /* duplicated body */ }
+  transform: makeTransform((doc) => ({
+    url: `/blog/${doc._meta.path}`,
+    tableOfContents: createToc(doc.content),
+  })),
 });
```

This removes ~40 duplicated lines and keeps the transform behaviour consistent across collections.

