review_comment:
![high](https://img.shields.io/badge/priority-high-orange)

The event listener is only removed when the 'updateToken' event is received. If the event is never received, the listener will remain active. Consider adding a timeout to remove the listener after a certain period to prevent potential memory leaks.

```javascript
    const eventHandler = (event) => {
      if (event.data.event === 'updateToken') {
        localStorage.setItem('authToken', `Bearer ${event.data.token}`);
        window.removeEventListener('message', eventHandler);
        clearTimeout(timeout);
        return resolve();
      }
    };
    const timeout = setTimeout(() => {
      window.removeEventListener('message', eventHandler);
      resolve();
    }, 5000); // Timeout after 5 seconds
```

