review_comment:
**suggestion:** Provided OtpOptions parameter is not used in the URI generation.

If the intent is to allow customization through the OtpOptions, consider integrating the options into the generated URI. Otherwise, documenting that the parameter is currently ignored would improve clarity.

Suggested implementation:

```csharp
    public string GenerateOtpUri(OtpOptions? options = null)
    {
        // If options is null, set default values
        options ??= new OtpOptions
        {
            Label = "BootstrapBlazor",
            Secret = "OMM2LVLFX6QJHMYI",
            Issuer = "Simulator",
            // Providing default values for additional parameters
            Period = 30,
            Digits = 6,
            Mode = OtpHashMode.Sha1
        };

        var uri = $"otpauth://totp/{Uri.EscapeDataString(options.Label)}?secret={options.Secret}&issuer={Uri.EscapeDataString(options.Issuer)}";

        // Append the period if set
        if (options.Period > 0)
        {
            uri += $"&period={options.Period}";
        }

        // Append the digits if set
        if (options.Digits > 0)
        {
            uri += $"&digits={options.Digits}";
        }

        // Append the algorithm (hash mode)
        uri += $"&algorithm={options.Mode.ToString().ToUpper()}";

        return uri;
    }

```

Review the OtpOptions class to ensure that it contains the properties: Label, Secret, Issuer, Period, Digits, and Mode. Adjust the default values as needed to adhere to your expected behavior in your codebase.

